**Platform type:** Platform is intentionally setted to be a character body 3D, so in this example, it is a character body 3D on top of another character body 3D.

### What is added

A new boolean variable — **`platform_velocity_correction_beta`**. When enabled, it fixes the one-tick lag by:

- Adding sorting logic for objects with equal `physics_priority`: when both the platform and the rider share the same priority (e.g. both at `0`), the fix checks which object is `is_on_floor()` on the other — and ensures the **platform is always processed before the object standing on it**. This also works with **multiple levels of nesting**.
- Reading the platform's velocity **as it was updated in the current tick**, rather than using the platform's velocity from the previous tick (which is the current behavior in the unmodified engine).

### Priority handling

| Scenario | Behavior |
|---|---|
| Platform has lower `physics_priority` than the rider | Fix runs platform first, lag resolved |
| Both have the **same** `physics_priority` (e.g. `0`) | Fix **auto-sorts** platform to higher priority regardless of scene tree order |
| Rider has lower `physics_priority` than the platform | Fix is not applied, lag exists because we trust the physics_priority higher than the auto-sorting mechanism. (auto-sorting mechanism ignored) |

